-- title:
--   Supersingular primes contain every minimal prime of (varpi) on X₀(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbf{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K_2$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 (M * p)))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the subfield of $L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbf{Q} \to L$ of the subfield of $\mathbf{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbf{Q}$ by the quotients $P_f/P_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms $f, g$ of equal weight on $\Gamma_0(Mp)$ with $P_g \ne 0$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$, with $K_2$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K_2$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K_2$ be nonzero with image in $L((q))$ the coefficientwise image of the rational $q$-expansion $q^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}(q)$ of the modular invariant. Write $B =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A K₂ j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142) for the $A$-subalgebra of $K_2$ consisting of the elements integral over the subalgebra $A[j]$ generated by $j$, and `jChartFin` for $j$ viewed in $B$. Let $y \subseteq B$ be a prime ideal containing the image of $\varpi$ and such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon B \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has trivial $p$-torsion among its affine points. Then every minimal prime $\mathfrak{p}$ of the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of $\varpi$ satisfies $\mathfrak{p} \subseteq y$.
--
--   In classical terms: both branches of the fibre at $p$ of the integral model of $X_0(Mp)$ over $\mathbf{Z}_{(p)}[\zeta_p]$ — the closure of the cuspidal branch and its Atkin–Lehner twist, each a copy of $X_0(M)$ — pass through every supersingular point, so that no minimal prime of the special fibre avoids a supersingular prime. It is used for the corresponding assertion on the $j$-finite chart of $X_1(Mp)$ ([`ModularCurve.XOneP.le_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.le_of_mem_minimalPrimes_span_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin_x1_mul)) and in the identification of supersingular places on the two-chart integral model of $X_0(Mp)$ ([`ModularCurve.XZeroP.exists_mem_ssPlaces_ringHom_eq_residueFst_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin_twoChartIntegralModel_gamma0_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XZeroP.exists_mem_ssPlaces_ringHom_eq_residueFst_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin_twoChartIntegralModel_gamma0_mul)).
